                  <msItem>
                     <title>Missale</title>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">The three British Library MSS. Add. 29704--5
                        &amp; 44892 have been constructed as one. The Glasgow MS. BD.19.h.9 (now
                        Euing 26) was part of the same book. Another volume of cuttings has been
                        found in London, Private Collection, 2.</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Two vols. of borders, initials, etc., now
                        reconstructed. Cf. E. Millar, Engl. Illum. MSS., 2. 271, and M. Rickert,
                        "The reconstruction of an English Carmelite missal", Burlingon Magazine 67
                        (Sept. 1935) 99--113: "made probably for Whitefriars, London"; M. Rickert,
                        "Reconstruction of an English Carmelite missal", Speculum 16 (1941)
                        92--108.</note>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
